---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Paul Digital Privacy Policy"
  description="Read the Paul Digital Privacy Policy for information about data processing, permissions, advertising, billing, and app-specific practices."
  canonicalUrl="/privacy/"
>
  <article>
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal information</span>
        <h1>Paul Digital Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>Effective Date: <time datetime="2026-10-09">October 9, 2026</time></p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="content-section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <p>
          Paul Digital develops Android applications and practical digital tools. This Privacy
          Policy explains how information may be processed when you use this website or a Paul
          Digital app that links to this policy. Individual apps and website features may differ;
          processing depends on the feature and service being used.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          This policy applies to your use of the Paul Digital website and to Paul Digital apps
          that link to this policy. Each app may have different features, permissions,
          advertising, billing, storage, and third-party services. Review the relevant Google
          Play listing and any disclosures shown in the app you use. This policy does not mean
          that every app handles information in the same way.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information and Data Processing</h2>
        <p>
          The information involved depends on how you use the website or a particular app.
          Depending on the feature, it may include information you enter or content you choose
          to process. Any processing by website hosting or app-integrated services also depends
          on the relevant service and its disclosed practices.
        </p>
        <h3>A. Information processed locally on your device</h3>
        <p>
          Depending on an app’s features and your actions, information processed on your device
          may include text you enter, files or images you select, audio or video files, app
          settings, conversion history, or other locally stored records. These are examples only;
          an individual app does not necessarily process each type of information listed.
        </p>
        <p>
          When an app processes information locally, that information may remain on your device
          unless you explicitly share, upload, or otherwise transfer it using the app or your
          device.
        </p>

        <h3>B. Information processed by third-party services</h3>
        <p>
          Some apps may use third-party services for functions such as Google Play distribution
          and billing, or advertising through Google AdMob when integrated. The services used
          depend on the app and its published configuration. A third-party service may process
          information under its own privacy terms and policies.
        </p>

        <h3 id="analytics">C. Website analytics (Google Analytics)</h3>
        <p>
          With your permission, this website uses Google Analytics 4, a service of Google, to
          measure visits and understand which pages are used. Analytics is off until you choose
          Accept in the banner; if you decline, Google Analytics is not loaded. You can change
          your choice at any time using the “Analytics choices” link in the footer.
        </p>
        <p>
          When enabled, Google Analytics may collect page addresses and titles, referrer,
          approximate location, browser and device information, and interaction events, and may
          set cookies or similar identifiers. Google Signals and ad personalization are turned
          off. The file names, file contents and image metadata of files you process with our
          tools are handled in your browser and are not sent to Analytics. See
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            how Google uses data from sites that use its services
          </a>.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Some Paul Digital apps may display advertisements using Google AdMob. Not every app
          contains advertising. If AdMob is enabled in an app, Google and its advertising
          technology may process information in connection with advertising in accordance with
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Google’s Privacy Policy
          </a>
          and other applicable Google policies. Premium versions or purchases may remove
          advertisements where applicable.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Google Play Billing</h2>
        <p>
          Some apps may offer optional in-app purchases or premium products through Google Play
          Billing. Purchases are processed by Google Play, rather than directly by Paul Digital.
          The availability of purchases depends on the particular app.
        </p>

        <h2>5. App Permissions</h2>
        <p>
          An app requests permissions when needed for its functionality. Depending on the app,
          permissions may relate to photos, media or files; the camera; network or Wi-Fi
          information; notifications; or other device capabilities. Permissions depend on each
          app’s functionality. You can review and manage permissions in Android settings, subject
          to the options available for your device and Android version.
        </p>

        <h2>6. File and Content Processing</h2>
        <p>
          Some apps process content you choose, which may include images, PDF files, audio,
          video, or text. The types of content and the way it is processed differ by app.
          A file being processed by an app does not by itself mean that the file is uploaded to
          a server. Check the relevant app listing and in-app disclosures for details about that
          app.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Data Storage</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on the app, information may be stored locally on your device to provide app
          functionality. Examples may include settings, preferences, recent files, locally
          generated documents, and application state. You can generally manage or delete locally
          stored content through the app or your Android device, depending on the app and the
          type of content.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Depending on the app and its features, information may be shared with or processed by
          third-party service providers for functionality, advertising, billing, security, or
          another purpose disclosed for that app. The services and information involved vary by
          app; review its disclosures and the applicable third-party policies.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Children’s Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          Paul Digital apps may be intended for different audiences; this policy does not state
          that every app is designed for children. Apps intended for general audiences are not
          knowingly designed to collect personal information from children in violation of
          applicable laws.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Security</h2>
        <p>
          Reasonable measures are used to protect information handled by Paul Digital apps and
          services. No electronic system or method of transmission or storage can be guaranteed
          completely secure.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>
          Retention depends on the type of information and the specific app. You may generally
          delete locally stored files or data through the app or your device. For information
          processed by third-party services, retention is governed by the applicable third
          party’s policies.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
          Some apps may use third-party services, which can include Google Play for app
          distribution or billing and Google AdMob for advertising where integrated. The services
          used vary by app. For information about Google’s data practices, see
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            Google’s Privacy Policy
          </a>.
        </p>

        <h2>13. App-Specific Information</h2>
        <p>
          Because Paul Digital publishes different types of applications, individual apps may
          have different permissions, features, advertising behavior, storage behavior, and
          third-party services. The table below summarizes the currently published apps. Actual
          behavior depends on the specific app and its published version. Consult the relevant
          Google Play listing and applicable in-app disclosures for current app-specific
          information.
        </p>
        <div
          role="region"
          aria-label="App-specific privacy information"
          tabindex="0"
          style="max-width: 100%; overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 1rem;"
        >
          <table style="width: 100%; min-width: 42rem; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left;">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">App</th>
                <th scope="col" style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Purpose</th>
                <th scope="col" style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">File access</th>
                <th scope="col" style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Advertising</th>
                <th scope="col" style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Billing</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
                  Image to PDF Converter Offline
                </th>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Image/photo to PDF conversion</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">User-selected images/files as required by the app</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Only if enabled in the published version</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Only if offered in the published version</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">
                  WAV to MP3 Converter
                </th>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Audio conversion</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">User-selected audio files as required by the app</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Only if enabled in the published version</td>
                <td style="padding: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid var(--border);">Only if offered in the published version</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          App-specific disclosures may be updated as new applications are published. Apps that
          are not yet published are not listed here as currently available apps.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          This policy may be updated when apps, services, legal requirements, or data practices
          change. The effective date at the top of this page indicates when this version took
          effect. Please review this page for the current version.
        </p>

        <h2>15. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, app support, bug reports, or other inquiries about this
          policy, contact Paul Digital at
          <a href="mailto:askpaulonline@gmail.com">askpaulonline@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
